This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: if your outermost armor is blessed, there should be a 50% chance
that a bare-handed hit by a undead/demon will deal 1d4 damage to it
--iron_angel

[2]: Tossing food at some unintelligent creatures (such as pears to
bachulitheria) may have a *chance* of taming them. --TheShrewdDude

[3]: Likewise, tossing metal to metallivores should have a chance of
taming them, as well. (The rust monster eats the blessed greased
rustproof +8 Stormbringer!) --TheShrewdDude

[4]: Artifacts should blast monsters of the wrong alignment that pick
them up. --TheShrewdDude

[5]: When you play the passtune at the drawbridge, you should hear 5
gears turn. --BenUrban

[6]: Stun should make scrolls etc do different things, similar to
confusion. This would also entail needing to be able to stun oneself a
bit more reliably somehow. --JoshJ

[7]: Jumping over a shark needs a YAFM. --ilya86

[8]: Parched conduct: You must not drink from potions, fountains,
sinks, or other sources of liquid refreshment. --TheShrewdDude

[9]: Zapping a pool of water with a means of teleportation might cause
it to appear elsewhere, as with the effect of an overflowing fountain.
--TheShrewdDude

[10]: ^^ "On top of your head" is a valid teleportation destination
--xarann

[11]: By the same logic, certain, non-fixed traps (basically, beartraps
and land mines) should be teleported if they are hit with a spell of
teleportation, even if they are in their deployed form. --TheShrewdDude

[12]: Stuffing a bag of holding into another bag of holding should
result in one, double-thick bag of holding. Certainly the bag just
expands until it can't expand anymore, right? --TheShrewdDude

[13]: Why not have fast food joints? If you defined TOURIST, then you
might find some new shops around town. McRodney or Ogre King, anyone?
--TheShrewdDude

[14]: Vowel-ChangeR: As a member of the R group, this creature will
change the vowels in items that you possess. Your wand of striking
might become a wand of stroking; that long sword might become a lung
sword. Imagine the possibilities! --TheShrewdDude

[15]: The quantum mechanic deliberately jumps into a polymorph trap! --
More -- The quantum mechanic's shape suddenly seems uncertain!
--BenUrban

[16]: Eating a disenchanter corpse sets your Pw to 0. --ek|M

[17]: Putting an orange in a pit (on a lit square) causes a tree to
appear after enough turns --zid

[18]: Spellbooks of cure blindness should be able to be read while
blind. Braille, anyone? --TheShrewdDude

[19]: Diluted (full|extra) healing potions don't add to maximum HP
(nerfing alchemy). --ekiM

[20]: New #conduct- Mute: Player cannot chat, (cast spells?), or read
scrolls. --JoshJ

[21]: If you put enough rocks in a pit (100 maybe?), it should be
filled. --BenUrban

[22]: Pointy thrown or fired weapons should sometimes stick to monsters
until they die. --Mumbo


Individual ideas may have contributions from multiple authors/editors,
but we currently only record the nickname of (usually) the original
author.



